native aa64: SIGNED sub-word (int8/int16) value cells miscompile under register pressure. The ~60 sub-word shift locals (sweeping 10 count types) force spills, and the aa64 backend corrupts spilled int8/int16 values — output is correct for the first ~9 checks, then wrong once spilling starts (positional, not count-type-specific). Isolated int8<<int8 etc. pass; uint8/uint16 and int32+ value cells pass (only SIGNED sub-word). A native-aa64 sub-word spill/reload codegen bug, NOT the shift logic (host-int / VM / gen2 all pass). See claude-todo.md.
